hello and welcome to math simplified i'm  dr umar malik and i'm back today with  another interesting video  in our previous videos we have discussed  about smoking and how to detox your  lungs from the damage caused by smoking  we also discussed about a few natural  ways to help your lungs recover from the  damage caused by smoking  i encourage you to watch that video  first  the link to that video will be displayed  in the top left corner of the screen  right  now our lungs are essential for our  survival so taking good care of them is  really important for us but elements  like smoking and living in a polluted  environment affects them very negatively  before we go deeper into the video i  would like to remind all of you that  smoking is considered as a global  pandemic as tobacco use kills 5 million  citizens globally every year  the world health organization projects  the number of deaths will double just 15  years from now  as i mentioned in my previous videos  smoking is a leading cause of  preventable deaths in the world  if you smoke you are effectively  decreasing your life by 10 years or more  but smoking and pollution are not the  only reasons why lung diseases are  getting very common  lots of people find it hard to breathe  because there is inflammation in their  lungs this can be due to diseases like  asthma chronic obstructive pulmonary  disease pulmonary fibrosis or even from  lung cancers  while foods have not been proven to heal  or treat such diseases research has  found that lifestyle changes like  following a healthy diet and getting  enough exercise can definitely help in  lung health and recovery  a healthy well-balanced diet goes a long  way to keep your body strong including  your lungs  in this video i will tell you about some  super foods that if included in your  diet can substantially boost your lung  recovery and eventually give you  healthier lungs so let's begin  the number one food we are gonna discuss  is turmeric  turmeric is a well-known superfood  turmeric's potential as a powerful  antioxidant and anti-inflammatory food  has been recognized by researchers for  decades now  curcumin is a pigment found in turmeric  that not only gives it its  characteristic bright hue but also  provides a range of health benefits  turmeric has been studied in relation to  arthritis eye conditions cancers heart  diseases alzheimer's disease and much  more  recently a study involving  2478 people was done to find a  correlation between turmeric use and  lung function  the results showed that turmeric intake  was associated with improved lung  function  also the improved lung function was  proportional to the curcumin intake  level  in fact high curcumin intake in smokers  was associated with up to 9.2 percent  better lung function compared with  smokers who did not consume curcumin  so adding turmeric to your diet might  just be the boost your lungs need for  good health it will not only add flavor  to your diet but also bring a wholesome  goodness as well  if you'd like to know more about  turmeric make sure to subscribe to our  channel as we are going to upload a  video on this topic very soon  the number second superfood for lung  health is beetroot  beet root which is a reddish delightful  salad we all love is a superfood  beet and beet greens have been shown to  benefit lung function  this is because beet is packed with  nitrates and nitrates are very important  for healthy arteries  they relax the blood vessel walls which  decreases blood pressure and effectively  increases oxygen intake all of which can  help someone struggling to breathe  this is especially important in people  with lung conditions like copd and  pulmonary hypertension a disease that  causes high blood pressure in the lungs  beets are also packed with vitamins and  nutrients that can promote lung health  like magnesium vitamin c carotenoids  antioxidants and potassium  now why potassium is important is a very  simple answer potassium helps in  reducing water retention which prevents  fluid buildup in the lungs  the most common source of potassium is  bananas spinach broccoli mushrooms beets  and other green leafy vegetables  so make sure to include these foods in  your diet  number three on the list are vitamin c  rich foods  in our previous videos we have talked  about how oxidative stress damages the  organs its blood supply and hinders the  recovery process  antioxidants are the antidote to this  damaged one of the most important yet  easily available source of antioxidants  is vitamin c  vitamin c is a water-soluble nutrient  that acts as a powerful antioxidant  getting enough vitamin c is especially  important for those who smoke  according to a 2015 study in people with  adequate vitamin c intake lung function  is favorable even in smokers  cigarettes are terrible for your body  since they have a negative effect on  your antioxidant source so it's  important that people who smoke  to increase their intake of vitamin c in  their diet  a 35 milligram per day vitamin c intake  is shown to be beneficial  some of the richest sources of vitamin c  include peppers plums  cherries guavas blackcurrant parsley  spinach kiwis and  obviously lemons and citrus fruits like  oranges  and berries  if you would like to know more about how  vitamin c helps your body boost your  health and more you can click the banner  above or go to the link in the  description below we have made a video  on this topic and i'm sure you will like  it  number four on the list are carotenoids  and other antioxidants  carotenoids are the pigments in plants  of red yellow and orange color you may  ask why a color giving pigment comes on  this list for lung beneficial foods  well carotenoids are vital antioxidants  for humans let me give you an example  lycopene  lycopene is a carotenoid antioxidant  which is associated with improved lung  health and what is the richest source of  lycopene the bright red lucious tomatoes  eating tomatoes can help reduce  inflammation in people with asthma and  lung disease  a survey was done in 2015 to find a link  between the dietary intake of  antioxidants and 10 year lung function  they found that eating plenty of  antioxidants like those present in  fruits and tomatoes was linked to  healthier lungs even when you're getting  older they also stated that this  association was especially strong in  smokers who had quit a 2019 study was  done among the patients with asthma at  al-shifar medical complex in gaza strip  palestine its aim was to identify major  dietary patterns and their association  with the level of asthma in those  patients  they found that a prudent pattern of  diet was associated with a lower  prevalence of asthma this prudent  pattern was characterized by high intake  of whole grains  beans and legumes  fish and shellfish products vegetables  tomatoes fruits and healthy vegetable  oil  all of these are highly dense sources of  helpful carotenoids  some of the other antioxidant rich foods  that you can start including in your  diet are pumpkins  pumpkins contain a wide variety of lung  health promoting plant compounds  these include carotenoids such as  beta-carotene lutein and zeanthene  blueberries are also rich sources of  anthocyanins including malwaredin  cyanidine peonitin delphinidin and  petunin  these are good to consume if you want to  keep your lungs healthy  cabbage especially red cabbage is also a  rich source of anthocyanins additionally  it is a rich source of fiber which also  helps to detox the body  ademy beans are a great source of  isoflavones eating high isoflavone diets  may reduce the chance of getting various  diseases including copd a 2010 study was  done to find a relation between lung  function changes and traditional  japanese food the japanese diet is high  in soy products and fish which are  excellent sources of isoflavones and  helpful fatty acids  the results state that isoflavone also  improved the shortness of breath  number five on the list are coffee and  cocoa  coffee is a wake up drink for billions  of people worldwide every morning its  effect are attributed to caffeine which  is found in coffee tea cola drinks and  cocoa a recent research has shown that  caffeine might also act as a wake-up  drug to boost your lung health  a 2010 research studied the effect of  caffeine in people with asthma  the results stated that caffeine appears  to improve airway function modestly for  up to 4 hours in people with asthma  this is attributed to its ability to  dilate airways and blood vessels which  improves airflow and oxygen exchange  leading to decreased symptoms even  though the effects are temporary  it is here that we can also talk about  the benefits of cocoa  if you are a health conscious person  then you may have heard about the health  benefits of cocoa and cocoa products  like dark chocolate  they contain a compound called  theobromine which helps to relax the  airways in your lungs a 2019 study was  done to find a link between cocoa intake  and overall health in university  students  the author suggests that cocoa's  potential health benefits are due to its  high polyphenol content  this is attracting much attention due to  its potential cardio protective  anti-inflammatory anti-obesity and  neuroprotective actions which are  positively reflected in peoples who  regularly consumed cocoa  now what about our lungs well to find  this out in 2018 an extensive research  was carried out in more than 55 000  adults  the results of this study were published  in a paper known as dietary intake of  flavonoids and ventilatory function in  european adults  the study showed that increasing the  consumption of dietary sources of  flavonoids can contribute to maintaining  lung function  and can also prevent its decline  the study found that those who consumed  more flavonoids found in foods like  chocolates for example had stronger  lungs versus those with lower intake  high time you start indulging on  chocolate but be careful excess of  everything is harmful  well friends with this we come to the  end of this video i hope i have given  you some new and exciting facts and  knowledge if you like today's video  don't forget to share it with your  friends and family if you are new to our  channel consider subscribing if you like  our content we admire simplified always  appreciate your support and feedback  consider becoming a member of our  youtube channel or patreon community  as always take care and i'll see you in  the next video
 

